{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope\/MiddlewareReducer","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MiddlewareReducer","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a Reducer conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MiddlewareReducer"},{"type":"text","text":", the generated Store class will implement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HierarchialScopeMiddleWare"},{"type":"text","text":" and observe events from child scopes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"updateSubstate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the child’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"update()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has already processed the event —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"childState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the child’s state once that update finished, not a preview of what’s about"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to happen. This mirrors "},{"code":"statoscope-zustand","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s "},{"code":"onChildAction(action, childState)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"documents the same thing: “called with the action and the child’s already-updated state.”"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The event is always forwarded to the child; there is no way to intercept or veto it, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none is needed — by the time a parent’s ancestors get a look, the child has already safely"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied the event to itself, so a parent reaction that goes on to destroy or replace that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"child subtree can never race with a stale event still being delivered into it. That race"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SubstateOutcome.intercept"},{"type":"text","text":" case that existed solely to guard against it) doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exist in this ordering."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"parentState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is read-only — "},{"code":"updateSubstate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" decides, it never mutates. To react, return a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delegated "},{"code":"When","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; it is sent to the parent’s own "},{"code":"update()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the only place "},{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is ever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutated and the only place a reaction can also enqueue effects. Return "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for no reaction."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Example:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Reducer","struct ParentReducer: MiddlewareReducer {","    struct State: Injectable {","        @SubState var child: ChildReducer.State?","        var delegatedTasks: [String] = []","    }","","    enum When {","        case childDelegated(String)","    }","","    static func updateSubstate<Child: Reducer>(","        _ childType: Child.Type,","        childState: Child.State,","        childWhen: Child.When,","        parentState: State,","        dependencies: ReducerDependencies","    ) throws -> When? {","        \/\/ Child.State and Child.When are tied — both belong to the same Reducer","        guard let when = childWhen as? ChildReducer.When else { return nil }","        switch when {","        case .taskCompleted(let task):","            return .childDelegated(task)","        }","    }","","    static func update(_ when: When, state: inout State, ...) throws {","        switch when {","        case .childDelegated(let task):","            state.delegatedTasks.append(task)","        }","    }","}"]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MiddlewareReducer","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:10Statoscope17MiddlewareReducerP","title":"MiddlewareReducer","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MiddlewareReducer"}],"modules":[{"name":"Statoscope"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Protocol for Reducers that want to react to child scope events","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope\/MiddlewareReducer\/State","doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope\/MiddlewareReducer\/When"],"title":"Associated Types","generated":true,"anchor":"Associated-Types"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope\/MiddlewareReducer\/updateSubstate(_:childState:childWhen:parentState:dependencies:)"],"title":"Type Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/statoscope\/middlewarereducer"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Statoscope/documentation/Statoscope/MiddlewareReducer/updateSubstate(_:childState:childWhen:parentState:dependencies:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"updateSubstate(_:childState:childWhen:parentState:dependencies:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Called AFTER a child scope’s own "},{"code":"update()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has processed an event."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope\/MiddlewareReducer\/updateSubstate(_:childState:childWhen:parentState:dependencies:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"updateSubstate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Child","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Child","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"childState","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Child","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Statoscope7ReducerP5StateQa","text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"childWhen","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Child","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Statoscope7ReducerP4WhenQa","text":"When","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"parentState","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Statoscope17MiddlewareReducerP5StateQa","text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dependencies","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Statoscope19ReducerDependenciesP","text":"ReducerDependencies","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"When","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Statoscope17MiddlewareReducerP4WhenQa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/statoscope\/middlewarereducer\/updatesubstate(_:childstate:childwhen:parentstate:dependencies:)","required":true},"doc://Statoscope/documentation/Statoscope":{"title":"Statoscope","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A lightweight library for managing state in iOS applications, designed with simplicity, testability, and scalability in mind.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope","url":"\/documentation\/statoscope","role":"collection"},"doc://Statoscope/documentation/Statoscope/MiddlewareReducer":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/statoscope\/middlewarereducer","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope\/MiddlewareReducer","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MiddlewareReducer","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MiddlewareReducer","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MiddlewareReducer","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol for Reducers that want to react to child scope events"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Statoscope/documentation/Statoscope/MiddlewareReducer/State":{"role":"symbol","required":true,"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"State"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope\/MiddlewareReducer\/State","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/statoscope\/middlewarereducer\/state","title":"State","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Statoscope/documentation/Statoscope/MiddlewareReducer/When":{"role":"symbol","title":"When","type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Statoscope\/documentation\/Statoscope\/MiddlewareReducer\/When","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"When"}],"url":"\/documentation\/statoscope\/middlewarereducer\/when","required":true}}}